I don't get the WARNING by simply browsing the exported directory, or 
touching a file on it, e.g.:
  # touch /var/cache/distfiles/xz-5.8.3.tar.gz

But as soon as I access a file's contents, e.g. via:
  # gzip -l /var/cache/distfiles/xz-5.8.3.tar.gz
I hit the WARNING.

This happens only for the 1st time I access a file on the share. 
Subsequent accesses to the file or other files on the share don't 
provoke these warnings again.

The host sharing the exported directory runs kernel v6.18.48. The 
clients accessing it v7.3-rc1, but also v7.2.x, v7.1.x. Can't remember 
whether earlier kernels were affected too. On the host I don't get any 
dmesg the time the WARNING happens on the clients.

Full kernel dmesg and kernel .config attached.

